3,"Oceanic music and dance - Polynesian, Melanesian, Aboriginal | Britannica",https://www.britannica.com/art/Oceanic-music/Regional-styles-and-traditions,"August 2, 2002 - In the mid-20th century the Dutch scholar Jaap Kunst attributed the tiled type found in the interior of western New Guinea, the Torres Strait, and Australia to “a people who, without doubt, emigrated from Asia to Australia—where the majority of them finally settled—by way of New Guinea and Torres Strait.” Triadic melody style has been connected with speakers of non-Austronesian (Papuan) languages in New Guinea and elsewhere in Melanesia, while pentatonic structure is described as an element of Austronesian culture in Melanesia.",Kumalu,Austronesian
